WEBVTT

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.500
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.500
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.790
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.790
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:34.180
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:34.180
the only thing I truly have

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:39.470
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:39.470
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:44.810
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:44.810
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:50.070
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:50.070
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:55.450
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:55.450
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.540
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.540
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:07.080
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:07.080
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.170
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.170
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.470
hibike kono koe yo

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.470
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:22.720
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:22.720
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:28.400
namida kareru made

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:28.400
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.440
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.440
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:38.780
namida hareru made

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:38.780
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.790
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.790
though I may lose my way,

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.620
egakikake no ima

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.620
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.130
kizamu

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:54.880
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.420
akashi

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.880
kono te de

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:00.680
The Southpaw in Distress

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:00.680
The Southpaw in Distress

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.230
Chavez!

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.660
Say something!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.480
You all right?

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.710
Chavez!

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.260
Okay, okay.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.280
I'm fine.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:29.100
What's your date of birth and your address?

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:34.210
October 05, 1983, and Church Street, Columbus City.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.560
Thank goodness.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.400
Do you want to sit out just in case?

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.730
Nah, I'll be fine.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.780
This is nothing.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.510
Shigeno, I'm ejecting you for that dangerous pitch.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.160
Hey, Shigeno!

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.290
You have to leave.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.980
S-Sure.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.670
Get lost!

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.440
You're unbelievable!

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.090
What's your problem?!

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.610
You suck!

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.340
This took a turn for the worse.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.180
We stirred up his problem in the worst way possible.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.990
It's unfortunate for him, but he might never get back on the mound, you know.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.310
What's happening to me?

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.870
In my entire baseball career,

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.060
I've never pitched a ball...

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.270
at a batter's head.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.360
Never at someone's head!

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.760
And that's the game!

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.870
5-7!

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.100
That was the Hornets' fourth consecutive loss.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.290
Shigeno takes a loss after leaving the mound in the fifth inning.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.350
He's only played two games,

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:01.110
but he's already falling behind in the majors.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:01.110
I wonder if that batter is doing okay.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.570
Goro must be traumatized too.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:07.350
What happened to Honda was a rare case, but...

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:11.410
I'm more worried about Goro.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:18.870
Anyway, I'm glad you're all right.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.980
You bet I am!

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:22.090
You take care.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.200
Yeah, good night.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.670
Hi, Mr. Chavez?

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.750
Oh, you're...

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.020
How's your head feeling?

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.100
I'm sorry.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.690
It wasn't intentional at all.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:40.670
Please forgive me.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.400
Oh, is that what you're here to say?

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.820
Are you stupid?

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:52.070
I've heard that you're expected to bow and apologize when you hit someone with a pitch in Japan,

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.580
but it's different here.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.620
If you get hit, you get a free pass to first base,

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.250
and the pitcher faces penalties or ejections.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.650
Don't worry about it.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.210
Plus, it's obvious that it wasn't intentional or done in anger,

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:07.670
and if it were, I'd probably be pissed out of my mind even if you apologized.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:12.760
Given how you were pitching today, I knew it wasn't intentional.

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:16.640
Well, I really appreciate you saying that,

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:20.980
but throwing a pitch anywhere near someone's face is an unforgivable mistake.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.260
After all, it could be lethal.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.110
Besides, even if you're feeling fine,

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:30.400
a hit to the head could easily affect your batting.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.280
Hey, kid!

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.910
Don't take me so lightly!

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:38.810
I'm not cowardly enough to let a hit to my head slow me down.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:44.420
No matter how many pitches hit me, I'll keep standing in the batter's box.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:48.610
I worked my ass off for a spot on the major league roster, and there's no way in hell I'm giving it away to someone else!

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.180
R-Right.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.560
Well, just don't worry about it.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.800
Good luck in your next game, rookie.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.290
Hi.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.540
Oh, Shigeno.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.090
It's Stacy.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.780
Are you still at the stadium?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.170
Hm? Yeah.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.430
I have something important to say.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.700
Can you come to my office?

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:37.660
What?!

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.080
You forced him to keep pitching?!

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:42.540
Yeah.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.150
Don't "yeah" me!

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:48.940
Then it's partly your fault that it happened!

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.610
Sanders.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.970
Don't be so hard on Keene.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:57.280
He thought it was for the best.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.440
If Shigeno has the yips, this would've happened sooner or later.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:09.110
In any case, I told the boss and the coach that what happened today was my fault.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:15.530
But even they're feeling anxious about how easily Shigeno falls apart.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.970
Shigeno seemed to have gotten called to the coach's office,

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.180
so I'm sure something happened.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.090
Shigeno...

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:34.390
Chips?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.430
No, the yips.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.410
There's no way that's possible.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:47.940
I've already recovered from the loss at the World Cup.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.300
Shigeno!

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.630
You there?

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:56.580
It's me, Sanders.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.520
I want to talk to you for a bit.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.390
Can I come in?

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:06.340
Sure.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.570
It just wasn't your day today.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.600
Don't worry, it happens to everyone.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:24.410
Besides, I heard Keene made you pitch when you were coming down with a cold.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.020
Then it's not your fault.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.540
Keene was apologizing about it, too.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.990
It's not really Keene's fault.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.590
This is my problem.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:40.410
Besides, I don't have any cold symptoms.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:46.330
The boss just told me a terribly bad joke.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:48.340
The boss?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.150
Yeah.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:54.940
Apparently, they think I've got some yips disease.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:58.860
He said if the symptoms show up again in the next game,

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.720
he'll send me to the minors to fix it.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:04.940
I see...

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:12.590
I don't care if it's the yips or the pops. I'm not buying it!

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.000
Just watch.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:20.660
I'll show them that I'm not some chicken or cripple in the next game!

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:52.290
Ball.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.250
Ball four.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.180
What the hell are you doing?

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:04.240
You've walked two runs in already!

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.590
I knew he wasn't anything special.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.300
He couldn't get a single out,

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:47.350
and they're taking him out after he gave up a single and five walks in the first.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:52.180
Shigeno, what's gotten into you?

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:59.550
For God's sake, what is wrong with him?!

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:04.240
He's an unbelievable disappointment!

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.290
As stated, there are only night games being held today.

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:15.880
They'll begin at around 6:00 PM.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:19.820
On another note, we've just received some unfortunate news from the majors.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:23.800
Shigeno appeared on the mound for the third time today, pitching for the Hornets,

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:27.290
yet he wasn't at his best, giving up five walks without getting a single out.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:30.890
After the game, the team announced that he's been demoted to the minor leagues.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.560
After his phenomenal performance at the World Cup,

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:35.980
he was put in the spotlight at the start of the season.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:35.480
I had a feeling something was up.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:37.130
It really wasn't anything trivial.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.310
It has ended rather unfortunately.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:39.880
Goro...

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:47.560
I knew it.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:52.950
I knew something was up as soon as he left the mound in his debut game.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:55.480
It looked a bit like he had the yips.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:58.860
W-Wait a minute. What's the yips?

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:03.050
It's an illness that plagues athletes.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:06.220
Under the fear and anxiety of making an error,

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.430
their motor skills fail and cause even more mistakes.

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:16.210
Some are even forced to retire due to the illness, unable to escape the hellish cycle.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:18.650
No way!

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.170
That can't possibly be it...

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:26.240
Well, he's usually overconfident and arrogant,

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.530
so it's hard to believe he'd fall victim to the illness.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:32.060
I sure hope he doesn't have the yips.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:53.180
Geez!

00:12:58.310 --> 00:12:59.060
You idiot!

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.110
Why won't you give me a call or anything

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.820
when you're feeling down?

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:17.250
See ya.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.250
Give my best to the Bats.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:23.250
Don't worry, you're just going there to get fixed up a bit.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:26.300
You'll be back to the majors in no time.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.670
That's right!

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:30.950
Go pitch some perfect games and make your way right back.

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:32.720
Sure.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:53.430
You better come back.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:01.790
Isn't that...?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:06.840
Man, I knew I'd seen you before.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.610
You're Shigeno from the Hornets!

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:11.970
Oh, I get it.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.350
You got demoted for pitching so horribly yesterday.

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:19.100
Is that why you're sitting on this bus like a loser?

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.090
What?

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:24.230
That's enough.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.730
Put yourself in his shoes.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:26.610
What?

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.150
Put myself in his shoes?

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:33.160
He should put himself in the shoes of the Hornets' fans!

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:37.230
I've been their fan ever since I was a kid!

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.410
Yet what was wrong with you?

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:43.670
Oh, the "golden rookie" from Asia?

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:47.000
You're just a yellowbelly who can't even pitch a strike!

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.990
Don't even think about wearing the Hornets' green uniform!

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:51.200
What'd you say?!

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:55.870
I said that's enough, you brainless idiot!

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.470
I'm sorry.

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:00.140
My husband's still a little drunk.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:01.180
Shut up!

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:02.790
I'm not drunk!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:07.650
But you know, we really had high hopes for you.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:13.450
You pitched all those 100 mph pitches at the World Cup and had that no-hitter in your debut.

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.720
We all thought our team had gained an amazing player.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:22.660
Even yesterday, we decided to come to an away game just to see you pitch,

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:24.980
so my husband's a little irritated.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:27.500
He doesn't mean any harm.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:28.940
I hope you'll forgive him.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.010
I see.

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:34.870
Well, I'm sorry about that.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:40.970
I don't need an apology, so get your act together and come back.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:43.540
If you pitch the way you did in your debut,

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:46.150
I'll definitely cheer you on.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:49.570
Thanks.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:54.850
Welcome back...

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:58.770
wouldn't exactly be the right thing to say, huh?

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:00.330
Yeah.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:04.080
I didn't want to have to come back here again,

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:09.690
but I guess I couldn't get pumped without you cheering from the dugout in your cosplay.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.610
Well, it was my fault for not being able to produce results.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:16.260
If I just keep pitching and get back up to snuff,

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.800
they'll call me back up in no time.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.830
I can start pitching tonight, Boss.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.560
The starting pitcher, a relief pitcher... I'll do...

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:28.250
You're rather bold considering how you pitched in your last game.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:32.730
Unfortunately for you, you won't be playing any games for a while.

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:34.930
That's the order from the Hornets.

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:36.530
What?

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:38.870
Wh-What do you mean?

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:42.100
There's no point in you pitching in your current condition.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:46.500
You know that you might have the yips, don't you?

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.960
The yips is a psychological problem.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.480
If you don't fix that,

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.300
you'll really have to consider retirement.

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:07.690
That was a great nap.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:13.360
We're pretty far into the country.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:16.050
Where are you taking me anyway?

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.280
We're almost there.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:19.970
How much longer, Gordon?

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.620
Just ninety-seven more miles.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:23.680
How are we "almost" there?!

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.410
Give me a break.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.040
The sun's gonna go down.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:29.560
I won't be able to get back before the game.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.130
Did you forget what I said?

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.800
You don't need to worry about the game.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:38.990
Besides, you'll be staying where we're headed right now.

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:42.370
What?!

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:57.760
I guess this is it.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.900
It's so cute!

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.170
No, no, McGwire.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:14.670
Don't hurt him.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:17.590
Welcome.

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:19.420
I take it you're from the Bats.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:20.740
Come in.

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:30.390
I'm sorry.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:33.770
He said he would be home by five.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:35.270
No, it's fine.

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.410
Hello?

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:47.370
Hey, what in the world is this place?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.790
Who do you want me to see?

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:54.670
I kept you in the dark so you wouldn't make things difficult,

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:55.570
but I think I can tell you now.

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:59.380
This... is where Dr. Oliver lives.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:00.950
He's a sports psychologist.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.880
Wh-What?

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.780
Sports... cyclone?{acting dumb, etc; he actually says "saikoro" which means "die/dice" as in the six sided cube w/ dots, but the important thing is that the english sounds similar to... "psycholo" I guess. Change to something better if you know one.}

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:11.140
He's a psychological therapist who specializes in helping athletes.

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:13.230
In order to cure your yips,

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:17.730
the Hornets' management referred us to someone who's well known in this field.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:21.610
I'm so sorry.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.200
My husband will be a bit longer.

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:30.750
You spend hours and hours to bring me to the middle of nowhere,

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:32.310
and I'm here for therapy?!

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:34.250
You must be kidding!

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:39.150
I'm not some weakling who needs to rely on some pee serum!

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.590
Hey, wait!

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:41.490
Shigeno!

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:43.490
Give me a break!

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:47.910
Hey, Gordon!

00:19:49.140 --> 00:19:50.180
Start the car!

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:50.960
We're going back.

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:54.640
I only follow her orders.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:56.850
You're not going anywhere, Shigeno!

00:19:58.310 --> 00:19:59.440
No, thanks!

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:01.990
I'll hitch a ride somewhere and go home!

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:03.280
Geez!

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.820
What is up with him?!

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:06.870
Making an escape...

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:08.240
Shall I pursue him?

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:10.600
I can apprehend him rather easily with the car.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.870
No, it's fine.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:15.620
We'll do it another day.

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:19.530
I can't let him meet the doctor like that.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.970
This is ridiculous!

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.680
I don't have time for therapy!

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:31.760
If I did, I'd be better off pitching in real games as treatment anyway!

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:36.100
Hey!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.520
Could you stop, please?

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:43.690
Thanks, man.

00:20:43.690 --> 00:20:46.070
I'm headed back to Memphis.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:49.320
Think you can give me a ride in that general direction?

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:52.330
Oh, sure.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.000
Hop in.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:54.700
Awesome!{lit: "I'm in luck" or something like that}

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:55.730
Thanks a lot.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:58.790
I owe you!

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.510
H-Huh?

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:09.840
Didn't I just come this way?

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.490
Just recently...

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:15.390
there was a burglary in a nearby town.

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:18.170
It's not very safe here, so I suggest you be careful.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:24.650
If you ask me, hitchhiking's absolutely out of the question.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:35.500
Well, I'll be going home once I find Shigeno.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:38.040
I'm really sorry about what happened today.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:41.750
Just a minute.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:43.860
My husband is just pulling up.

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:52.490
Welcome back.

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:55.220
Thanks, honey.

00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:58.460
You must be Ms. Alice from the Bats.

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:01.350
I'm Oliver, a psychologist.

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:04.070
I'm sorry to have made you wait.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:05.730
Not at all.

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:09.390
I have to apologize to you too.

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:11.110
Apologize?

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:14.870
You see, the player I talked to you about...

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:17.750
He's run off.

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:19.080
Oh.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:20.860
Don't worry about that.

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:23.530
Shigeno?

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:26.800
He was a little noisy, so I shut him up.

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:30.050
You can drive back home now.

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:34.140
I'll take care of him for a while.

00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:36.760
You can leave everything to me now.

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:58.810
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:58.810
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:04.190
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:04.190
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:10.410
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:10.410
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:15.200
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:15.200
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:21.790
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:21.790
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:27.670
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:27.670
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:33.510
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:33.510
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:38.930
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:38.930
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:38.930 --> 00:23:45.400
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:38.930 --> 00:23:45.400
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:50.650
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:54.120
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:54.120
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:56.580
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.120 --> 00:24:02.960
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:56.580 --> 00:24:02.960
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:06.790
sotto

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:06.790
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:14.970
Preview

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:14.970
Preview

00:24:10.690 --> 00:24:12.590
Some weird old man abducted me,

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:15.510
and now I'm doing some stupid treatment.

00:24:15.950 --> 00:24:18.120
Like I give a damn about the yips.

00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:20.350
I'll be back on the field in no time.

00:24:21.290 --> 00:24:24.660
Next time, on Major: The Fruits of the Treatment.

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:29.060
Next Time

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:29.060
Next Time

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:29.110
The Fruits of the Treatment

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:29.110
The Fruits of the Treatment

00:24:24.660 --> 00:24:26.790
Run toward the stage of your dreams!
